00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:17.029 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  my name is han wai  and i am the creative director and  co-founder of lancervie kny  an award-winning industrial design  studio based between italy and singapore  francesca and i met 14 years ago in  einhoven the netherlands  while we were doing our masters i was  the first batch of design singapore  scholars  and this european experience opened my  eyes and mind to what design can be  can do and can become we've designed for  internationally renowned brands like ms  living divani capellini to name a few  and in 2020 after 10 years in the  business we launched nena  our first chair with the iconic italian  brand zanota  whose pieces are found in museums  worldwide it's an incredible landmark  moment for us  i have lived in the netherlands germany  hong kong shanghai  copenhagen and now i'm based in  singapore how does my life here inspire  me as a creative person  as a designer i grew up in panam valley  and its architecture by tanjing siong  has affected my spatial sensing and  mental navigation  there are many ways to navigate  landscape and many entry points to the  next location  discovery is made fun and engaging  patan valley is a prime example of step  down architecture  where the building stepped down with the  slope side best of all the inherent  variety  in the build forms and building  orientations provide for surprises and  experiences  no one could plan for i love this green  corridor beside my place  because i'm running into nature and its  long straight route  allows me to effectively meditate  minding my breathing  watching where i land my feet  controlling my heart rate  and naturally curating my thoughts when  the green corridor is completed  which i cannot wait for it will be an  uninterrupted 24 kilometer green stretch  between woodlands  in the north and tanjung paga in the  south as a runner  this excites me to the core because it  will be such a scenic and culturally  rich experience to run through heritage  sites and suaves of undisturbed nature  it will be a magical example of  international city plan  that i'm sure will become a main artery  for the burgeoning numbers of bicycle  commuters too  running also helps me experience the  singaporean cityscape  in an entirely different way as opposed  to being a car  bus or train gardens by the bay always  instills a sense of awe in me especially  the cloud forest conservatory  with the 42 meter cloud mountain within  and whose signature supporting  structures i can run under like some  sci-fi futuristic city landscape  which this part of singapore is actually  and has served for backdrops for several  sci-fi tv serials and movies  it makes you realize the senses are not  that great it is a perception thing  and it's actually conquerable it's an  incredibly liberating realization  i love my taco teal especially philipp  saguero  the malia reaction due to the sugars in  the dark soy sauce and noodles  the brightness of the chives and my  goodness  the rich sweet runny yolk flip is a  genius  it's a carbonara thing in chagriday this  is his chakra  this man's an innovator a designer  and i also love natural wines we're  talking about being able to consume and  experience a location  a terroir from another place on earth  you are able to drink a winemaker's  philosophy as well  you are drinking authenticity and truth  straight up  this interior is that of a barcelonian  one easy laid back  you pick your wine off this gorgeous  wall not a wine list  you could start a conversation with a  fellow patron here  the interior is open planned with its  structures and services  intentionally bare the wine glasses have  no stems  you hold the glass more directly and the  food comes on small plates to encourage  tasting  and definitely sharing i'm also huge on  dim sum  because it reminds me of family time on  sundays  the design of the food informs how we  interact  behave feel and make memories  the interior is new southeast asian  chinese  where the design languages of our  culture have been re-interpreted  for the contemporary consumer and their  tastes  the main dining hall chairs are inspired  by archetypal rattan weave chairs  which lends an air of lightness being  transparent  and transparent the concept of life  is a new typology of work play and  living  we're talking about co-working and  co-living all in the same property  the ambiance is casual and energetic a  place where you can bump into people  new or old friends and connect the  public furniture  in life we designed were to encourage  spontaneous fun  as you would encounter your favorite  ride at the playground  the design journey is a marathon not a  sprint  the design process requires solitary and  deep thinking  and running helps me hone my focus but  also the active act of letting  non-essential thoughts go  and just be in the flow of the now the  act of creation  [Music]  a good design process is a mindful  rigorous marathon  running teaches me patience consistency  and resilience  the design journey is a marathon hence i  am a runner  you

